<b>S E T T I N G S

<c>[Dialog]
<c>->  [F2·Settings]

In the Settings-tab there are most of GoatPlayer's settings.
Use arrowLeft and arrowRight to modify the value of the selected item.
In some cases a Readline-dialog or a Find-dialog will be used to set the item's
value. (For some items, all possible values are printed in the status-bar.)

<b>List of all settings

<i>Repeat playlist
<i>Equalizer
<i>Progress-bars delay in milliseconds

<i>Open in Browser at ...
From some windows, it is possible to open the internet browser.
From the "Genres" window, the selected genre will be searched
for. From the "Artists" window, the selected artist will be searched for.
And so on. These settings define which internet sites will be opened when the
"Open in Browser" command is executed.

<i>Player: select the playing audiofile
This setting selects the new playing audiofile's line as it changes.

<i>Player: playing-line is blinking

<i>Play only the first N seconds [No/10/20/30]
This is used to play just the first seconds of each audiofile.

<i>Audio pitch correction [Yes/No]
When speed is different than 1, this corrects the pitch.
